    "html": "<figure><img src=\"assets/walkthrough/coordinate-projection.svg\" alt=\"Computed plots of a colored slab triangle before transformation, after translation by 300 centimeters, and after perspective projection to image coordinates.\" width=\"1040\" height=\"650\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Follow the red vertex: local (0,0,0) becomes world (300,0,0) cm. The camera at (250,0,400) looks along world −Z; this illustration defines positive camera depth along that forward direction, giving camera coordinates (50,0,400). It lands 30 pixels right of the image center. The green vertex is the prose’s local (100,0,0), now world (400,0,0). The triangles are computed from these coordinates. This is an original mathematical rendering, not an Unreal screenshot or an assertion about Unreal matrix storage order.</figcaption></figure>"
