    "after_contains": "The add path illustrates the handoff precisely.",
    "html": "<figure><img src=\"assets/walkthrough/thread-snapshots.svg\" alt=\"Three timeline lanes show the gate angle advancing first on the game side, then in the render snapshot, and later in a submitted GPU frame.\" width=\"1040\" height=\"590\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Read vertically at t2: gameplay has reached 60°, the prepared render snapshot shows 30°, and the illustrated GPU work still reads 0°. The angles visualize separate snapshots of the same object, not three gameplay gates. Publishing a change preserves the data already referenced by an in-flight frame; the exact amount of frame overlap is configuration-dependent.</figcaption></figure>"
