    "chapter": "a-material-is-a-surface-program",
    "after_contains": "Material instances reuse a parent material",
    "html": "<figure><img src=\"assets/walkthrough/material-response.svg\" alt=\"Three original software-rendered spheres show the same green material and lighting with narrow, medium, and broad specular responses as one roughness-like parameter changes.\" width=\"1040\" height=\"650\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Compare the highlight, not the sphere silhouette: the geometry, green base color, and illumination are identical. The pixels are computed by the included software renderer. Its simple exponent model is printed to make the demonstration reproducible; it is not Unreal’s microfacet BRDF or a measured comparison of Unreal roughness settings. The visual isolates the meaning of changing a surface response without moving a light or rebuilding a mesh.</figcaption></figure>"
