    "html": "<figure><img src=\"assets/walkthrough/courtyard-gbuffer.svg\" alt=\"Six computed images of the same courtyard show base color, world normals, ray depth, roughness, lamp visibility, and the final direct-lit result.\" width=\"1040\" height=\"795\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Choose a surface and locate it in all six panels. The checker pattern belongs to the paving’s base color; its upward normal has a different encoding; its shadow can change while those properties remain fixed. All panels use the same ray intersections. This original software renderer uses simplified direct lighting and a constant ambient term, with no GI; the panels illustrate logical values rather than Unreal’s physical GBuffer packing. The separate <a href=\"assets/walkthrough/courtyard-lit.png\">lit frame</a> is also available.</figcaption></figure>"
