    "html": "<figure><img src=\"assets/walkthrough/off-camera-shadow.svg\" alt=\"A plan-view camera cone includes a paving sample but excludes the gate above it. The lamp-to-sample ray intersects that off-camera gate, creating a shadow on the visible sample.\" width=\"1040\" height=\"630\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Trace the blue camera ray to P, then the gold lamp ray to the same P. Only the gold segment crosses the gate. Culling the gate from the main camera’s work is valid; deleting it from the persistent scene because of that culling would incorrectly remove the shadow. The drawing is a geometric example, not a measured Unreal shadow-map view.</figcaption></figure>"
