    "after_contains": "A ray intersection is only part of a lighting answer.",
    "html": "<figure><img src=\"assets/walkthrough/intersection-versus-cache.svg\" alt=\"A ray hits a triangle at 1,1,0; a separately parameterized four-unit card maps that point to 0.25,0.25 and then to a resident atlas region, while pink cells mark absent coverage.\" width=\"1040\" height=\"650\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The red point is a geometric hit. The green outlined atlas region is a separate parameterization used to retrieve cached information. A correct intersection does not guarantee that the selected card covers that surface with valid lighting. The printed card projection is illustrative; it deliberately distinguishes capture coordinates from the material’s authored UV coordinates.</figcaption></figure>"
