    "chapter": "deriving-an-arda-scene-from-the-courtyard",
    "after_contains": "Now edit one scanned point.",
    "html": "<figure><img src=\"assets/walkthrough/point-provider-revisions.svg\" alt=\"A point cloud sample moves beyond its old bound. A revision table advances the point buffer and bounds, marks optional derived triangles stale, and leaves an absent ray product absent; missing UV and tangent data force an explicit material fallback.\" width=\"1040\" height=\"710\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The red point moves, so both the point positions and the enclosing bound change. The right-hand entries distinguish an existing stale derived product from a representation that never existed. A material requiring UVs and a tangent basis cannot be satisfied by position-and-color records alone; a declared point-color fallback is honest and testable. The earlier lifetime rule still applies to the old allocation used by an in-flight frame.</figcaption></figure>"
